  "plan": {
    "goal": "Design a perfused lung alveolar-capillary barrier chip (A549) at very low physiological shear of 0.03 Pa (0.3 dyn/cm²).",
    "rationale": "Target shear 0.03 Pa matches the lung alveolar-capillary physiological anchor (~0.03 Pa) and sits within the A549 registry shear range (0.02–0.05 Pa). A 400×100 µm PDMS channel at 1.2 µL/min (computed via flow_rate_for_shear_stress with water-like medium viscosity 1e-3 Pa·s) delivers exactly 0.03 Pa. Reynolds 0.08 confirms laminar flow; residence time 40 s; pressure drop 12 Pa is trivially supplied by a syringe pump. A549 seeded at 10,000 cells/cm² (upper end of registry range) on the 0.08 cm² channel floor gives ~800 cells/channel. O2 supply (0.00024 µmol/min at air-equilibrated 0.2 mM inlet) is ~500× the estimated epithelial demand, so the low flow does not starve the cells. 16 biological replicates per group (perfused vs static control) detect a 1-SD difference at 80% power, alpha 0.05.",
